From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wbemprox: paging files from /proc/swaps, no invented identity strings (3526)

wbemprox: paging files from /proc/swaps, no invented identity strings; ntdll SMBIOS serials

Win32_PageFileUsage and the new Win32_PageFileSetting list the swap areas of the host (files, partitions, zram)
with AllocatedBaseSize/CurrentUsage in MB, names as paths on Z:; empty when there is no swap (the static
c:\pagefile.sys row is gone). BIOS, baseboard, ComputerSystemProduct and SystemEnclosure no longer make up
manufacturer/name/serial/version strings when the firmware has none (they are empty); ntdll's synthesized SMBIOS
no longer fills "System Serial Number", "Chassis Serial Number" or a board serial derived from the UUID.
Win32_OperatingSystem.Manufacturer stays "The Wine Project", the QuickFixEngineering entry stays as it was.
